--=-=-=

As requested by the kernel, I'm mailing you. Sound wasn't working on my
Toshiba P105-S6197, even with Linux 2.6.23-rc4. It is working since I
added acpi_osi=!Linux to the kernel's command line. Enclosed are files
that you may find helpful. I am using Debian's linux-source-2.6.22
package version 2.6.22-3.

Mark

